WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.330 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  God Jesus Voldemort Optimus Prime kylo  Ren Falkor Donald Trump what do they all  have in common well they're all  characters humans created to tell  stories and to answer big questions  whether you believe these characters are  real or not is up to you  this is exactly what having a belief  means there is no more evidence that God  exists or that Jesus was his son then  there is that Optimus Prime was a real  talking transforming robot or that  Falkor helped Atreyu stop the nothing in  the neverending story belief is the  question here a leap of faith is what  makes man believe in ideas he would  never accept if they were presented  outside the realm of religion if a  friend told me that LeBron James dunked  from half-court meaning he jumped all  the way from half-court to slam the ball  in the hoop with one jump I would ask  for video of this claim if my brother  told me that he could turn water into  beer I would demand that he do it in  front of me he not just give me some  water down Bud Light and take his word  for it  yet for some reason Jesus walking on  water or Moses talking to a burning bush  or Mohammed riding a winged horse to  heaven are things that were supposed to  take on faith if I told you right now  with all the credit I've gained from you  guys that I rode a winged horse to the  studio today you'd say that I was  totally bonkers and you'd be right  because the truth is that I wrote in on  Falkor who is a winged block dragon this  brings me to atheism the best definition  I've found for atheism is it is not a  denial of God's it is a lack of belief  in God this is an incredibly important  distinction to make an atheist isn't  denying that a god or gods exist an  atheist is just asking for evidence of  such an incredible claim all this really  means is applying the same standard of  belief and pretty much anything else you  do in your life to the biggest questions  of the  universe you don't just believe magical  pictures come out of your television  scientists and engineers created the  correct conditions for your TV to exist  you believe your TV is there and does  what it does because of the evidence  right in front of you you don't just  believe the audio coming out of your  iPhone is magical Apple elves living  inside that thing singing you know that  you downloaded the entire soundtrack to  Dreamgirls and sing it in your room  every night it didn't just magically  appear there the point here is that  believing in something without evidence  is up to you but it shouldn't trump  anyone else's belief in things that are  empirically provable if you find comfort  in believing in god or gods or the  spaghetti monster or whatever else is  out there then that's fine as long as  you don't push your beliefs on or kill  other people who believe in something  else again all the Atheist is saying is  I don't believe without evidence it  reminds me of this quote by the great  Carl Sagan extraordinary claims require  extraordinary evidence hearing that a  guy talked to a burning bush doesn't  prove anything other than that he might  be crazy or took some really great magic  mushrooms if he can prove it well then  we've got a whole other discussion on  our hands interestingly many polls show  that atheists are still one of the least  trusted or liked groups in the United  States while there are signs this is  changing there is still a ton of work  that needs to be done the atheists I  know are generally the most open liberal  decent folks out there I know there is a  push mainly on the left to demonize  atheists as Islamophobes or neo cons but  this is really just nonsense a phobia is  an irrational fear of something it is  not irrational to fear a set of ideas  which would have you killed as a  non-believer atheism also isn't a  political ideology once again it's just  a lack of belief atheists come in all  colors sexualities and nationalities  actually atheism is a great take down of  the barriers that often divide us as  people if we can start at a point in not  believing in ideas until they are proven  to be true then we can start having real  conversations about how to live as  people and to make our world a better  place this isn't to say that at least  from my view that all religion and  belief is bad in and of itself millions  of people have their beliefs and do  charity work care for the less fortunate  or help the needy in the name of their  religion could they do these things  without religion yeah probably but if  that helps them get there and then great  but when your beliefs impede on the  lives of other people I have a problem  with religion my guest this week are two  non believers but as far as I can tell  to pretty decent human beings David  Silverman is the president of the  American atheist and Paul Provenza is a  comedian director and outspoken atheist  we're going to discuss the good the bad  and the ugly about religion and about  atheism itself now if you'll excuse me  I'm going to ride a unicorn to  shangri-la where I'm playing bingo with  Frank Sinatra and Frodo Baggins  [Music]

